If the RRC message segmentation is enabled based on the field rrc-SegAllowed received in appLayerMeasConfig, and the encoded MeasurementReportAppLayer message is larger than the maximum supported size of a PDCP SDU (as specified in TS 38.323), the UE shall:

1. **Initiate the UL message segment transfer procedure** (as specified in clause 5.7.7), rather than submitting the MeasurementReportAppLayer message directly.
2. **Submit the MeasurementReportAppLayer message to lower layers for transmission**, upon which the Application Layer Measurement Reporting procedure ends.

In effect, instead of sending the oversized MeasurementReportAppLayer message directly to lower layers, the UE hands it off to the UL message segment transfer procedure, which (per clause 5.7.7) segments the encoded RRC PDU based on the maximum PDCP SDU size, minimizing the number of segments, and constructs ULDedicatedMessageSegment messages by:

- Setting **segmentNumber** to 0 for the first segment and incrementing it for each subsequent segment;
- Setting **rrc-MessageSegmentContainer** to contain the corresponding segment of the message;
- Setting **rrc-MessageSegmentType** to **lastSegment** for the final segment, or **notLastSegment** otherwise;
- Submitting all generated ULDedicatedMessageSegment messages to lower layers for transmission in ascending order of segmentNumber, upon which the UL message segment transfer procedure ends.

Based on the specification, a UE in (NG)EN-DC only executes a subclause of clause 5 in TS 38.331 when the subclause meets **at least one** of the following three conditions:

1. **Referred to from a subclause under execution** — either in TS 38.331 itself, or in TS 36.331 (i.e., the subclause is invoked/called by another subclause that is currently being executed);

2. **Applies to a message received on SRB3** — provided SRB3 is established (i.e., the subclause governs handling of a message that arrived over SRB3);

3. **Applies to field(s), IE(s), UE variable(s), or timer(s)** in TS 38.331 that the UE is configured with (i.e., the subclause governs a configured element of the UE's current configuration).

Additionally, when the UE does execute such a subclause under these conditions, it must also follow the requirements in clause 5.1.2, along with all other applicable subclauses of TS 38.331 relevant to the messages (including processing time requirements), fields, IEs, timers, and UE variables indicated in the subclause under execution.

When the received sl-MeasConfig includes sl-MeasIdToRemoveList, the UE shall perform the **sidelink measurement identity removal procedure** (as specified in clause 5.8.10.2.2). Specifically, for each sl-MeasId included in the received sl-MeasIdToRemoveList that is part of the current UE configuration in VarMeasConfigSL, the UE shall:

1. **Remove the entry** with the matching sl-MeasId from the **sl-MeasIdList** within VarMeasConfigSL;
2. **Remove the NR sidelink measurement reporting entry** for this sl-MeasId from the **VarMeasReportListSL**, if included;
3. **Stop the periodical reporting timer** and **reset the associated information** (e.g., sl-TimeToTrigger) for this sl-MeasId.

Note: The UE does not treat the message as erroneous if sl-MeasIdToRemoveList includes any sl-MeasId value that is not part of the current UE configuration (i.e., such values are simply ignored, guarded by the "Configured sl-MeasId condition").

When the UE prefers to temporarily reduce the maximum aggregated bandwidth of FR1, it shall:

- **Include `reducedMaxBW-FR1`** in the OverheatingAssistance IE;
- **Set `reducedBW-DL`** to the maximum aggregated bandwidth the UE prefers to be temporarily configured across all **downlink** carriers of FR1;
- **Set `reducedBW-UL`** to the maximum aggregated bandwidth the UE prefers to be temporarily configured across all **uplink** carriers of FR1.

This configuration is only applicable when the UE experiences internal overheating and is initiating transmission of the UEAssistanceInformation message to provide overheating assistance information.

If the received **measConfig** includes the **measIdToRemoveList**, the UE shall perform the **measurement identity removal procedure** as specified in **5.5.2.2**.

Specifically, per that procedure, for each **measId** included in the received **measIdToRemoveList** that is part of the current UE configuration in **VarMeasConfig**, the UE shall:

1. Remove the entry with the matching **measId** from the **measIdList** within **VarMeasConfig**;
2. Remove the measurement reporting entry for this **measId** from the **VarMeasReportList**, if included;
3. Stop the periodical reporting timer, or **timer T321**, or **timer T322** — whichever one is running — and reset the associated information (e.g., **timeToTrigger**) for this **measId**.

**Note:** The UE does not treat the message as erroneous if the **measIdToRemoveList** includes any **measId** value that is not part of the current UE configuration.
